The copy constructor was already close to minimal, so this change is small and the speedup is probably marginal.

- `values` is still copied in the initializer list, exactly as before.
- `stringIndexes` is now default-constructed and only copied when the source is non-empty. Copy-assigning into an empty vector gives the same elements as copy-constructing it, so behavior is unchanged.
- Most fields have no string indexes, so this skips some copy work in the common case.

```cpp
FieldBase::FieldBase(const FieldBase &field)
    : values(field.values)
{
    if (!field.stringIndexes.empty())
        stringIndexes = field.stringIndexes;
}
```